---
import banner from '../../content/blog/using-dspy/banner.png';
// Bench objects: Plate and Deck. Covers come from src/assets/covers via coverFor; glow from glowOf.
import { coverFor } from '../../utils/covers';
import { glowOf } from '../../utils/glow';
import Deck from '../ui/Deck.astro';
import Label from '../ui/Label.astro';
import Plate from '../ui/Plate.astro';
import PostCard from '../ui/PostCard.astro';
import Readout from '../ui/Readout.astro';

const eden = coverFor('9780143129486');
const dalio = coverFor('9781982160272');
const edenGlow = eden ? await glowOf(eden) : undefined;
const dalioGlow = dalio ? await glowOf(dalio) : undefined;
const demo = [
	{ cover: eden, alt: 'East of Eden cover', glow: edenGlow },
	{ cover: dalio, alt: 'Changing World Order cover', glow: dalioGlow },
	{ cover: undefined, alt: '', glow: undefined },
];
---

<section class="objects" aria-labelledby="objects-h">
	<Label as="h2" id="objects-h">Objects</Label>

	<div class="group">
		<Label as="h3">Plate</Label>
		<div class="row">
			<figure><Plate src={eden} alt="East of Eden cover" /><figcaption>image</figcaption></figure>
			<figure><Plate src={eden} alt="East of Eden cover" glow={edenGlow} /><figcaption>glow</figcaption></figure>
			<figure><Plate src={dalio} alt="Changing World Order cover" glow={dalioGlow} ratio="1/1" radius="md" /><figcaption>1/1, radius md</figcaption></figure>
			<figure>
				<Plate>
					<span class="type"><strong>East of Eden</strong><span>John Steinbeck</span></span>
				</Plate>
				<figcaption>typographic</figcaption>
			</figure>
		</div>
		<p class="note">
			One physical object: --elevation-object, a 1px inner hairline, a fixed ratio. glow is a colour sampled from the
			image at build time (glowOf), the one coloured halo; a parent raises it with --plate-glow-strength and swaps the
			shadow with --plate-shadow.
		</p>
	</div>

	<div class="group">
		<Label as="h3">Deck</Label>
		<Deck items={demo} class="demo" label="Demo deck">
			{(c: (typeof demo)[number]) =>
				c.cover ? (
					<Plate src={c.cover} alt={c.alt} glow={c.glow} />
				) : (
					<Plate><span class="type"><strong>Third</strong><span>Typographic</span></span></Plate>
				)
			}
		</Deck>
		<p class="note">
			{'<Deck items={xs}>{(x, i) => <Card />}</Deck>'}. Stacked at rest; while the Deck (host "self") or an ancestor with data-deck-host (host "ancestor") is hovered or
			focused, it fans in place like a hand of cards. Positions come from the item count (spread, angle, lift props); {'cycle={s}'} deals the front card to the back while untouched (SPRING_DEAL).
			The active card is chosen from the pointer's x over the deck's fixed footprint, so a moving card never changes
			the choice; it comes forward, straightens and lifts while the others recede. Springs: SPRING_LAYOUT on enter
			(40ms stagger), SPRING_PRESS on active changes. Set down: the hand gathers with the pile held a few percent high,
			then it drops with one small knock (SPRING_SETTLE). Reduced motion paints each pose instantly: the hand still fans and closes, it just does not travel.
		</p>
		<Deck id="demo-pull" items={demo} hold="pull" captions={demo.map((d) => ({ title: d.alt || 'Typographic' }))} class="demo" label="Demo pull deck">
			{(c: (typeof demo)[number]) =>
				c.cover ? (
					<Plate src={c.cover} alt={c.alt} glow={c.glow} />
				) : (
					<Plate><span class="type"><strong>Third</strong><span>Typographic</span></span></Plate>
				)
			}
		</Deck>
		<Readout follow="demo-pull" field="title" value={demo[0].alt} />
		<p class="note">
			hold="pull" draws the card under the pointer up and out of the pile, turned in perspective (books); the default
			hold="fan" spreads the hand sideways (index cards). A Readout with follow=&lt;deck id&gt; and field=&lt;caption key&gt; shows
			the held card's caption (the front card at rest) with no script: pass captions=&#123;[&#123; title &#125;, ...]&#125; to the Deck.
		</p>
	</div>
	<div class="group">
		<Label as="h3">PostCard</Label>
		<div class="row cards">
			<figure>
				<PostCard href="#" title="Using DSPy" description="Programming rather than prompting a language model." date={new Date('2025-03-02')} image={banner} />
				<figcaption>image</figcaption>
			</figure>
			<figure>
				<PostCard href="#" title="A post without a banner image" description="The title is set large on the card instead." date={new Date('2024-11-20')} />
				<figcaption>typographic</figcaption>
			</figure>
			<figure>
				<PostCard href="#" title="Using DSPy" description="Programming rather than prompting a language model." date={new Date('2025-03-02')} image={banner} size="sm" />
				<figcaption>size sm</figcaption>
			</figure>
		</div>
		<p class="note">
			One link, one index card: the card is the shadowed object (--plate-shadow, so a Deck lifts it) and its Plate gives
			up its own shadow. Banner on top, or the title set large with a mono date; then title and description, each
			clamped. bannerFor(post) finds a post's banner.
		</p>
	</div>
</section>

<style>
	.objects {
		display: grid;
		gap: var(--space-10);
	}
	.group {
		display: grid;
		gap: var(--space-4);
		padding: var(--pad-tile);
		border: 1px solid var(--border);
		border-radius: var(--radius-tile);
		background: var(--surface);
		color: var(--surface-foreground);
	}
	.row {
		display: grid;
		grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fill, minmax(8rem, 10rem));
		gap: var(--space-8);
	}
	figure {
		margin: 0;
	}
	figcaption {
		margin-block-start: var(--space-2);
		font-family: var(--font-code);
		font-size: var(--text-small);
		color: var(--muted-foreground);
	}
	.group :global(.demo) {
		--deck-max: 9rem;
		margin-block: var(--space-6);
	}
	.type {
		display: grid;
		align-content: end;
		gap: var(--space-1);
		height: 100%;
		padding: var(--space-3);
		font-size: var(--text-small);
		color: var(--muted-foreground);
	}
	.type strong {
		color: var(--foreground);
		font-weight: var(--weight-title);
	}
	.cards {
		grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fill, minmax(12rem, 15rem));
	}
	.note {
		max-width: 48rem;
		margin: 0;
		font-size: var(--text-small);
		line-height: var(--leading-ui);
		color: var(--muted-foreground);
	}
</style>
